# Rudolph van Richten (NPC rictavio, docs/voice/rictavio.md) at his own tower. He is only here if he left Vallaki
# (rictavio_gone: Lady Wachter's town): he came home to think, and has been ignoring his student on the doorstep.
# start: in the workroom. shore: at Ezmerelda's fire after the two of them are reconciled.

~ start
if not flag.van_richten_met_at_tower
set van_richten_met_at_tower
Narrator: At the workroom table, under a lamp, sits the showman from the Blue Water Inn without his feathers or his voice: a thin old man in shirtsleeves, burn-scarred hands spread flat on a map of the valley.
Rictavio: You. How did you... Khazan. Of course. She found the name, and you walked in on it. I taught her to find things. I should have taught her to stop.
else
Rictavio: Still here. You've a talent for being where you shouldn't. I used to.
endif
if flag.van_richten_strongbox_opened
Rictavio: And you've been in my strongbox upstairs. Keep it. Where you're going, you'll need it more than I will.
endif
-> menu

~ menu
* [if not flag.ezmerelda_left_tower and tarokka.ally.npc != ezmerelda and not guest:ezmerelda] Ezmerelda is outside. She's been waiting for days. -> ezm
* [if guest:ezmerelda] She's right behind us, Doctor. -> ezm_here
* Why did you leave Vallaki? -> why
* [if tarokka.ally.npc == rictavio and not guest:rictavio] The cards still name you. Hunt with us. -> ally_again
* Goodbye. -> bye

~ why
if flag.vallaki_backed == "wachter"
Rictavio: That town chose its master, and I watched who helped it choose. I came home to think about whether anything in this valley is worth the trouble. I've been thinking for a week. It's gone very badly.
else
Rictavio: Reasons. Old ones. I came home to think. I've been thinking for a week, and it's gone very badly.
endif
-> menu

~ ezm
Rictavio: I know. I can hear her. Everyone within a mile can hear her.
Rictavio: I keyed the ward to her because everyone I have ever taught is in the ground, and she is the last. If she can't get in, she can't follow me where I'm going.
* [Persuasion DC 14] Then go down and tell her that yourself, while there's still someone to tell. -> reunite
* She'll get in eventually. You trained her. Better beside you than behind you. -> reunite
* It's your business, Doctor. -> menu

~ ezm_here
Narrator: Ezmerelda doesn't say anything. She just looks at him, with her hair still standing up from his ward, until he looks away first.
Ezmerelda: Hello, Rudolph.
Rictavio: Ezmerelda. You went through the ward.
Ezmerelda: You'd have done the same. You taught me.
-> reunite

~ reunite
set van_richten_reunited
set ezmerelda_trust += 2
set tower_ward_lowered
quest the_hunters_tower reunited
Narrator: He takes a long time to stand up, and longer to put his coat on, and longest of all on the stairs. From the lantern room above, something hums and goes quiet as he passes the hearth rod: the ward is down.
cutscene vr_reunion
if guest:ezmerelda
Narrator: The two of them go down the stairs together, arguing in low voices about whose fault the last twelve years were.
else
Narrator: A little later, through the window, you hear the shouting start on the shore. It goes on for a long time. Then it stops, and there is only the sound of two people sitting by a fire.
endif
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Look at him. Putting his coat on to go and get shouted at by his student. ...Lucky old man.
approve wren_featherfoot +2 liriel_dawnsong +1 kip_smudgewick +1 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You sent Van Richten down to his student
-> END

~ ally_again
if flag.den_children_freed
Rictavio: Eva's cards again. And I hear five children walked down out of the wolves' hills because of you. That counts for something. It counts for a great deal.
-> ally_join
elif flag.children_rescued
Rictavio: Eva's cards again. And the ravens tell me two children came home from a hags' mill on the Vallaki road, because of you. Hags don't give anything back. That counts.
-> ally_join
elif flag.argynvost_beacon_lit
Rictavio: Eva's cards again. And there's a silver light on the ridge over Argynvostholt, where there's been none for four hundred years. Somebody lit it. That counts for a great deal.
-> ally_join
endif
Rictavio: I told you once what I think of people who help this valley choose its masters. Words are cheap here. What have you done since?
* [Persuasion DC 15] We've learned. Come and watch us prove it. -> ally_join | ally_no
* Nothing yet. -> ally_no

~ ally_join
Rictavio: Very well. I'm too old to hunt alone, and you are much too young to be doing it at all. I'll come.
join rictavio
quest find_the_ally found
-> END

~ ally_no
Rictavio: Then come back when you have. I'll be here. I'm not going anywhere quickly these days.
-> menu

~ bye
Rictavio: Stay in the light where you can. And when you can't, stay together.
-> END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- At the fire, afterwards

~ shore
Rictavio: She has made me promise never to key a ward to anyone again. I have agreed to nothing. She knows I have agreed to nothing.
if not flag.ezmerelda_left_tower
Ezmerelda: He's agreed. He just doesn't know it yet.
endif
* [if tarokka.ally.npc == rictavio and not guest:rictavio] The cards still name you, Doctor. -> ally_again
* Goodbye. -> bye
